^api\.anthropic\.com$
^api\.openai\.com$
# Cloudflare Workers AI is reachable two ways and a deployment picks one with
# UL_CLOUDFLARE_WORKER_AI_ENDPOINT: api.cloudflare.com is the direct Workers
# AI API, gateway.ai.cloudflare.com is the AI Gateway in front of it. Both are
# listed because the endpoint is admin-configured free text, and getting this
# wrong is silent: policy.validate_cloudflare_endpoint accepts any
# *.cloudflare.com host, so a mismatch here fails at the proxy at runtime
# rather than at startup. Cloudflare is the default vision provider AND the
# only source of the image classifier, so a block here takes both out.
^api\.cloudflare\.com$
^gateway\.ai\.cloudflare\.com$
# ai-worker's own outbound tool calls (services/ai/tools/routing.py,
# weather.py) - added when those tools shipped; this file otherwise only
# ever needed ai-inference's provider hosts above. router.project-osrm.org is
# OSRM's public demo server, which is what UL_OSRM_BASE_URL falls back to. A
# deployment that sets that variable to a self-hosted OSRM has to add that
# host here too, or the assistant's distance_and_drive_time tool is the one
# caller that cannot reach it.
^router\.project-osrm\.org$
^api\.open-meteo\.com$
^api\.openweathermap\.org$
